@model Homespool.Host.Pages.PrinterFormFactor
@*
    A printer, in one of two form factors: an open bed slinger, or a closed box.

    Geometry is printer-bedslinger.svg and printer-enclosed.svg verbatim, inlined here rather than
    referenced with <img> - the same trade _BrandMark.cshtml makes, and for the same reason. Both
    render brand blue either way; what inlining buys is that currentColor resolves against the page,
    so the tile can lift the hue on a dark ground the way the link and navbar rules do. An <img>
    would sit at the one fixed blue baked into the file, which is right in light mode only.

    Three things are dropped from the source files on the way in. color="#278ED3", because it would
    pin the blue and defeat exactly that - site.css puts the colour back on .printer-shortcut-drawing
    instead. Then role="img" and its aria-label, because the plaque underneath already names the
    printer and says what it is doing; keeping them would make a screen reader announce "Bed slinger
    3D printer" before every name.

    OURS, and it has to be. Homespool talks to other people's machines and is an independent
    alternative to the software that ships with them - visual-identity.md §2 records the house blue
    being chosen as "not Prusa's orange" on exactly that reasoning. Both shapes are generic: many
    manufacturers build each.

    No ids, defs or masks, unlike the mark. This renders once per tile and ids are document-global
    once inlined; the mark's own comment records that trap, and six tiles on a page is where it would
    bite.
*@
@if (Model == Homespool.Host.Pages.PrinterFormFactor.Enclosed)
{
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 96 96"
         fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="6"
         stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
         aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" class="printer-icon printer-icon-enclosed">
        @* cabinet *@
        <rect x="14" y="9" width="68" height="76" rx="9" />
        @* lid seam and screen *@
        <path d="M14 23 H82" />
        <rect x="56" y="13" width="16" height="6" rx="2" stroke-width="3.5" />
        @* door window *@
        <rect x="25" y="31" width="46" height="42" rx="4" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.08" stroke-width="5" />
        @* gantry, carriage and nozzle *@
        <path d="M29 36 H67" stroke-width="4" />
        <rect x="42" y="37" width="12" height="7" rx="1.5" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.12" stroke-width="4" />
        <path d="M43 44 H53 V46 L49.5 51 H46.5 L43 46 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
        @* part on the bed *@
        <rect x="43" y="58" width="10" height="5" rx="1" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
        @* bed *@
        <rect x="30" y="63" width="36" height="5" rx="1.5" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.12" stroke-width="4" />
    </svg>
}
else
{
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 96 96"
         fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="6"
         stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
         aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" class="printer-icon printer-icon-open">
        @* base *@
        <rect x="18" y="75" width="60" height="9" rx="3" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.12" />
        <circle cx="69" cy="79.5" r="2.5" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
        @* gantry, broken where the bed passes *@
        <path d="M24 56 V27 H72 V56" />
        @* carriage and nozzle *@
        <rect x="38" y="30" width="20" height="12" rx="2" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.12" stroke-width="4" />
        <path d="M41 42 H55 V45 L50 51 H46 L41 45 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
        @* part on the bed *@
        <rect x="42" y="56.5" width="12" height="5" rx="1" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
        @* bed, resting on the base, wider than the frame *@
        <rect x="8" y="64" width="80" height="6" rx="2" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.12" stroke-width="5" />
    </svg>
}
